WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.548 --> 00:00:08.049
Pakistan is in crisis.

00:00:09.759 --> 00:00:11.553
The worst inflation in Asia,

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:14.264
mass protests,

00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:17.100
record energy prices,

00:00:17.976 --> 00:00:20.103
and an uptick in terror attacks.

00:00:20.895 --> 00:00:23.023
You’re talking about a very, very  

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:26.192
important regional market,

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.193
regional power.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.988
Pakistan’s economy is sinking.

00:00:29.988 --> 00:00:32.240
It has no option but to seek a bailout.

00:00:32.824 --> 00:00:34.951
Pakistan was once 
hailed as a country 

00:00:34.951 --> 00:00:38.121
that could be an economic rival 
to its neighbor India

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:41.916
but it's falling further and further behind. 

00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:46.629
The nuclear-armed country 
with 240 million people

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:48.131
 is living on the edge of ruin.

00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:53.595
Behind the scenes, its military is seen as holding sway over government policies. 

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:59.642
At the heart of it all, Pakistan is 
trapped in a cycle of borrowing 

00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:01.728
 that appears to have no end. 

00:01:02.312 --> 00:01:04.647
The IMF can’t let Pakistan sink.

00:01:04.647 --> 00:01:06.357
Pakistan sinks 
it will be chaos.

00:01:06.357 --> 00:01:08.526
And the world can’t 
afford this big a chaos.

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:18.620
Now the economic 
situation in Pakistan

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:19.954
has gone from bad to worse.

00:01:19.954 --> 00:01:21.664
Pakistan’s year-on-year inflation 

00:01:21.664 --> 00:01:24.667
hit a record level of 36.5%.

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.961
This is the highest-ever 
increase in nearly 60 years.

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:31.716
I’ve been working in this 
market for the last 28 years.

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.302
We are in trouble.

00:01:34.302 --> 00:01:38.515
Paying rent, bills, maintenance. Everything counts.

00:01:38.515 --> 00:01:41.893
Earlier, 40 to 50 customers 
used to visit us daily. 

00:01:41.893 --> 00:01:45.105
 But now, it’s down to 
two or three people, only.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.484
Even the three years 
during Covid was better.

00:01:51.486 --> 00:01:54.531
Pakistani people are very 
concerned at this point in time.

00:01:55.198 --> 00:01:57.617
You can see people are 
hopping onto boats

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:01.162
risking their lives to get to Europe somehow or another.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.332
People are borrowing 
money from loan sharks.

00:02:04.666 --> 00:02:09.170
And we have seen last year, at 
one point one-third of Pakistan

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:10.797
was flooded completely.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:15.844
And it led to losses 
and damages of $30 billion.

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:21.724
 I will never forget the 
climate-related carnage I saw. 

00:02:22.058 --> 00:02:28.314
Lives, homes, livelihoods, schools, hospitals, all obliterated.

00:02:29.357 --> 00:02:32.485
It’s expected that 
such natural calamities

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.112
will continue happening.

00:02:34.112 --> 00:02:36.781
And Pakistan does not have 
any funds to deal with it.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.368
Ahead of the general elections

00:02:40.368 --> 00:02:45.206
 all political parties have promised to take on politically difficult reforms

00:02:45.206 --> 00:02:49.794
which will help the country get on sustainable financial footing

00:02:49.794 --> 00:02:54.174
but none of them have been 
able to do so in the past.

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:55.842
We’ve been here before.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:59.220
And we have seen some of these bailouts actually get halted

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.598
over failure to meet certain conditions.

00:03:01.598 --> 00:03:07.770
It is very important that Pakistan sticks to the commitments under this program. 

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:11.816
 Meaning, don’t spend 
what you don’t have.

00:03:11.816 --> 00:03:13.985
Be prudent on tax collection.

00:03:13.985 --> 00:03:19.157
One of the big problems Pakistan 
has is very low tax to GDP.

00:03:19.782 --> 00:03:22.744
At the IMF we say if your tax to GDP

00:03:22.744 --> 00:03:24.996
is below 15% 

00:03:24.996 --> 00:03:26.831
you can’t really quite function 

00:03:26.831 --> 00:03:28.875
as necessary

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:33.421
to fund public services 
and the state expenditures.

00:03:33.963 --> 00:03:36.299
Is Pakistan’s debt sustainable?

00:03:36.966 --> 00:03:42.222
It is sustainable but it is 
borderline sustainability.

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:47.101
Pakistan’s inflows just do 
not cover its outflows.

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:49.896
Pakistan does not export enough.

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:52.982
Pakistan doesn’t have enough foreign direct investment coming in.

00:03:53.858 --> 00:03:56.069
Historically, this gap has been

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:58.947
filled by remittances, bailouts, 

00:03:58.947 --> 00:04:00.865
and direct injections of cash 

00:04:00.865 --> 00:04:02.450
from China and Saudi Arabia. 

00:04:09.457 --> 00:04:11.376
What we are short of is ideas. 

00:04:11.376 --> 00:04:13.211
What we are short of 
is rules and laws

00:04:13.211 --> 00:04:15.171
that are conducive to growth. 

00:04:15.171 --> 00:04:16.839
Unfortunately, we don’t understand that. 

00:04:16.839 --> 00:04:19.050
So we continue to go
to beg and borrow.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:22.262
We continue to build roads. 
We continue to build all these things 

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:25.348
which really do not 
give you quick growth.

00:04:26.557 --> 00:04:30.061
Nadeem Ul Haque worked for the International Monetary Fund

00:04:30.061 --> 00:04:31.229
 for 24 years. 

00:04:31.562 --> 00:04:35.066
Now he’s skeptical about the
IMF’s policies in Pakistan.

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:40.530
Pakistan is an IMF addict and 
the IMF is a Pakistan addict.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:43.658
We are both locked
in a death dance.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.244
The fault lies within. 

00:04:46.911 --> 00:04:51.040
The country’s political system 
is fraught with instability

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:56.421
with the military directly ruling for almost half of the nation's history 

00:04:56.421 --> 00:04:59.257
 and retaining outsized influence 

00:04:59.257 --> 00:05:04.178
even when democratically elected governments took power.

00:05:04.178 --> 00:05:07.932
The entire status quo, 
the entire political status quo

00:05:07.932 --> 00:05:09.559
is against me right now.

00:05:09.892 --> 00:05:12.770
Imran Khan’s government tenure was cut short when he was 

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:16.149
removed from power
 in April of last year.

00:05:16.524 --> 00:05:20.111
The government that replaced him oversaw a crackdown

00:05:20.111 --> 00:05:21.946
on Khan's political party,

00:05:21.946 --> 00:05:25.450
whose leaders are now being 
tried in military courts.

00:05:26.576 --> 00:05:29.162
The caretaker prime minister 
has previously said 

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:33.374
he will ensure fair punishment by law for those involved in violent protests.

00:05:34.792 --> 00:05:38.004
We tracked down a member of Imran Khan’s political party,

00:05:38.004 --> 00:05:42.216
the Pakistan Tehreek e-Insaf, 
or PTI.

00:05:42.216 --> 00:05:46.596
Can you tell the audience why 
are you hiding at the moment?

00:05:46.596 --> 00:05:52.393
There’s been a crackdown on PTI 
of the sort that unfortunately 

00:05:52.393 --> 00:05:55.396
only happens in 
countries like Pakistan,

00:05:55.396 --> 00:05:57.565
with a very clear 
and singular objective 

00:05:57.565 --> 00:05:59.108
of dismantling the party. 

00:06:00.068 --> 00:06:04.947
If we continue to go down the 
same path that we are going, 

00:06:04.947 --> 00:06:09.619
if we think we can fix this country without fixing the civil service,

00:06:09.619 --> 00:06:12.246
without fixing 
public sector contracts,

00:06:12.246 --> 00:06:14.415
without opening up 
to the free market, 

00:06:14.415 --> 00:06:17.251
without political 
and economic stability, 

00:06:17.251 --> 00:06:20.004
I don’t want to imagine 

00:06:20.004 --> 00:06:22.840
what 20 to 30 years down 
the line will look like.

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:29.931
Pakistan has had a history 
of violent terror attacks.

00:06:29.931 --> 00:06:34.102
Since the Taliban took 
over Afghanistan in 2021 

00:06:34.102 --> 00:06:37.772
 the situation 
has gotten much worse.

00:06:38.106 --> 00:06:43.611
Pakistan’s first priority is to prevent 
and counter all terrorism 

00:06:43.611 --> 00:06:45.988
from and within Afghanistan.

00:06:46.447 --> 00:06:52.412
Kakar’s caretaker government took over from Shehbaz Sharif in August 2023.

00:06:52.662 --> 00:06:55.373
We spoke to Sharif’s 
former economic adviser.

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:58.459
We have to widen the tax net. 

00:06:58.459 --> 00:07:02.338
We have to ensure that everyone is paying their fair share of taxes. 

00:07:02.338 --> 00:07:05.091
Our tax-to-GDP ratio 
is far too low.

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:09.762
Responsible privatization is 
the need of the hour. 

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:15.143
We can no longer afford as a 
country to continue bleeding

00:07:15.143 --> 00:07:17.854
in the manner that we have 

00:07:17.854 --> 00:07:20.398
on account of the 
state-owned enterprises. 

00:07:21.983 --> 00:07:25.736
In all this time, Pakistan has been living beyond its means. 

00:07:26.696 --> 00:07:28.406
All of this is creeping in.

00:07:28.406 --> 00:07:30.408
It is impacting people.

00:07:31.075 --> 00:07:35.163
That includes people like 
Jahanzaib, a stock analyst. 

00:07:35.163 --> 00:07:38.791
He has decided to leave 
Pakistan for good.

00:07:38.791 --> 00:07:41.544
Everyone I know, either they have moved out of the country 

00:07:41.544 --> 00:07:43.796
or they are desperately 
looking to move out.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:47.341
I was driven by the 
economic uncertainty, 

00:07:47.341 --> 00:07:49.760
the rapid PKR depreciation,

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:51.053
rampant inflation

00:07:51.053 --> 00:07:53.556
and uncertain political 
environment of the country. 

00:07:53.556 --> 00:07:57.185
Even though I had a 
very comfortable job, 

00:07:57.185 --> 00:08:04.066
I decided this was not what 
I want to go through everyday.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:10.323
Life in Pakistan will continue to be dominated by one institution:

00:08:10.323 --> 00:08:12.658
The Pakistan army.

00:08:12.658 --> 00:08:15.119
It has been a constant 
throughout decades  

00:08:15.119 --> 00:08:18.956
and continues to exert influence 
from behind the scenes.

00:08:19.373 --> 00:08:23.211
Some analysts say military interference stops overall progress 

00:08:23.211 --> 00:08:26.172
but then others argue 
it’s the only institution 

00:08:26.172 --> 00:08:28.799
that really can get 
things done in Pakistan.

00:08:31.636 --> 00:08:34.722
Hope seems to be running 
out for most Pakistanis. 

00:08:34.722 --> 00:08:36.599
But not for all.

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:41.646
We have to work together to convince our best and brightest

00:08:41.646 --> 00:08:46.526
that they have a future here, 
that we are intent on 

00:08:46.526 --> 00:08:49.612
 and are doing everything we can to make things easier for them.

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:55.034
I’m hopeful. 

00:08:55.034 --> 00:08:59.038
The majority of people 
I know aren’t hopeful.

00:08:59.038 --> 00:09:03.918
I’m hopeful because hope 
sustains the world.

00:09:03.918 --> 00:09:09.715
If I get disheartened, how will life be?  We need to push on.

00:09:10.508 --> 00:09:13.052
Pakistan will make it. 

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:15.596
The question is, when?

